Package: nano-blk-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: nano-blk-tools
Description: RAM-backed blk-mq block device driver (DKMS source)
 nano_blk is a small block device that keeps its data in RAM, one page at
 a time, allocated on first write.  It supports discard and write-zeroes and
 fails writes with EIO when the system is short of memory instead of invoking
 the OOM killer.
 .
 This package ships the module source and lets DKMS build it for every
 installed kernel, including kernels installed later.

Package: nano-blk-tools
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: data-integrity checker for block devices
 blkcheck issues random O_DIRECT writes, reads and discards against a block
 device and checks every read against an in-memory model of what the device
 must contain.  It ends with a full read-back of the device.
 .
 It is used by the nano-blk autopkgtest and works on any block device.
 It overwrites the device.
